name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA MICHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAKURA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUSHITA ELECTRIC INDUSTRIAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASANO, TOMOHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA, MICHIHIRO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ASAKURA HIROYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SASANO TOMOHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANAKA YASUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA MICHIHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ASAKURA, HIROYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SASANO, TOMOHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANAKA, YASUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAGATA, MICHIHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coupling lens (104) used for coupling the emerging light beam emerging from a semiconductor laser (101) to an optical fiber (108). The coupling lens (104) comprises a single lens integral with a diffraction lens composed of concentric ring bands on the plane of incidence or plane of emergence of the single lens. The diffraction lens has a positive refractive power. The relief function of the diffraction lens is generally an isosceles triangle. The depth W of the relief function satisfies the inequalities (1) 0.6 &lt;/= W(n-1)/ lambda  &lt;/= 1.0 where n is the index of refraction of the lens material, and  lambda  is the wavelength of the semiconductor laser. When the coupling lens is used for a semiconductor laser module, the output power of the module can be so controlled as to conform with the safety standards even if the attenuation film, polarizer, or optical fiber comes off without using any control circuit for automatically stopping the lasing of the laser.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une lentille de couplage (104) utilisée pour coupler à une fibre optique (108) un faisceau lumineux émergeant d'un laser à semiconducteur (101). Cette lentille de couplage (104) comprend une lentille unique à laquelle est intégrée une lentille de diffraction, composée de plusieurs bandes annulaires concentriques placées sur le plan d'incidence ou sur le plan d'émergence de ladite lentille, cette lentille de diffraction présentant un pouvoir de réfraction positif. La fonction relief de cette lentille de diffraction est généralement un triangle isocèle, la profondeur W de cette fonction relief vérifiant la relation (1): 0,6&lt;/=W(n-1)/ lambda &lt;/=1,0, dans laquelle n représente l'indice de réfraction de la lentille, et  lambda  désigne la longueur d'onde dudit laser à semiconducteur. Une fois la lentille de couplage utilisée dans un module laser à semiconducteur, la puissance de sortie de ce module peut être régulée de manière à respecter les normes de sécurité, et ce même si le filtre affaiblisseur, le polariseur, ou la fibre optique se détache sans utiliser aucun circuit de commande pour arrêter automatiquement l'action du laser.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>